 line←pattern RemoveHtmlTags_ line;mask;starts;segs;bool
⍝ Removes all HTML tags from a single `line` but leaves inline code alone.
⍝ What inline code actually is gets decided by MarkAPL itself: that way this agrees with
⍝ whatever MarkAPL is going to make of the very same line later on.
 :If 0<≢line
     mask←##.MarkAPL.GetMaskForCode line            ⍝ 1 for every character that is code
     starts←1,2≠/mask                               ⍝ A new piece starts whenever the mask changes
     segs←starts⊂line
     bool←0=starts/mask                             ⍝ Only what is not code is scanned for HTML tags
     (bool/segs)←{pattern ⎕R'\0' '\0' '\0' ''⊣⍵}¨bool/segs
     line←∊segs
 :EndIf
⍝Done
